    <section class="slide" data-title="Framework to research question" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From explanation to inquiry</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Let the framework sharpen the question</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Deductive use</h3><p>An existing theory supports propositions or hypotheses that the study tests.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Sensitising use</h3><p>A framework directs initial attention without fixing what qualitative inquiry must find.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Generative use</h3><p>Patterns in data support refinement or development of a conceptual or theoretical account.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Name the role of the framework. Do not claim to “use” a theory if it never shapes the question, evidence or interpretation.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>讓框架使研究問題更精準</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>演繹用途</h3><p>既有理論支持研究要檢驗的命題或假設。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>啟發用途</h3><p>框架引導初步注意，但不預先規定質性研究必須發現甚麼。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>生成用途</h3><p>資料模式支持修訂或發展概念／理論解釋。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">清楚說明框架扮演的角色。若理論從未影響問題、證據或詮釋，便不應聲稱研究「使用」了該理論。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research design and its components" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research architecture</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>A design coordinates the whole study</h2>
          <blockquote class="design-architecture-question">How will this study obtain evidence capable of answering the question and supporting the intended claim?</blockquote>
          <div class="component-grid architecture-components" aria-label="Eight decisions coordinated by research design">
            <article><span>01</span><strong>Purpose and problem</strong></article>
            <article><span>02</span><strong>Framework and assumptions</strong></article>
            <article><span>03</span><strong>Research questions</strong></article>
            <article><span>04</span><strong>Intended claims</strong></article>
            <article><span>05</span><strong>Design family and timing</strong></article>
            <article><span>06</span><strong>Cases, participants or data</strong></article>
            <article><span>07</span><strong>Sampling and access</strong></article>
            <article><span>08</span><strong>Quality and ethics</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway design-architecture-takeaway">A design is not simply “qualitative,” “quantitative,” a survey or an interview. Changing one decision may require changes elsewhere; alignment is a property of the system.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究設計協調<br />整項研究</h2>
          <blockquote class="design-architecture-question">本研究將如何取得能夠回答問題並支持預期主張的證據？</blockquote>
          <div class="component-grid architecture-components" aria-label="研究設計協調的八項決策">
            <article><span>01</span><strong>目的與研究課題</strong></article>
            <article><span>02</span><strong>框架與假設</strong></article>
            <article><span>03</span><strong>研究問題</strong></article>
            <article><span>04</span><strong>預期主張</strong></article>
            <article><span>05</span><strong>設計類型與時序</strong></article>
            <article><span>06</span><strong>個案、參與者或資料</strong></article>
            <article><span>07</span><strong>抽樣與進入研究場域</strong></article>
            <article><span>08</span><strong>研究品質與倫理</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway design-architecture-takeaway">研究設計不只是「質性」、「量化」、問卷或訪談。改變一項決策，可能需要同時調整其他決策；對齊是整個系統的特性。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Methodology, design and methods" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Pause · predict · reveal</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Three related decisions</h2>
          <p class="decision-instruction">Read each question first. Commit to an answer, then open the card.</p>
          <div class="decision-reveal-grid">
            <details class="decision-reveal" name="decision-level-en">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">Worldview</span><h3>Methodology</h3><p>What counts as knowledge, and how can we know it?</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>Broad and philosophical.</strong> The worldview and principles guiding how knowledge is produced.</p><p class="decision-examples">Positivism · interpretivism · constructivism · pragmatism</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="decision-reveal decision-reveal--centre" name="decision-level-en">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">Blueprint</span><h3>Research design</h3><p>How will the study be structured to answer the question?</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>Strategic and structural.</strong> The plan connecting questions, evidence, comparison, timing and inference.</p><p class="decision-examples">Experiment · descriptive survey · correlational study · case study</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="decision-reveal" name="decision-level-en">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">Tools</span><h3>Research methods</h3><p>Which procedures will generate and analyse the required evidence?</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>Specific and practical.</strong> The procedures and techniques used to generate and analyse data.</p><p class="decision-examples">Questionnaire · interview · observation · statistical analysis</p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
          <div class="connected-example">
            <div class="connected-example-head"><span>One study, three aligned choices</span><p><strong>Example question:</strong> How satisfied are secondary students with AI-supported feedback?</p></div>
            <div class="example-chain" aria-label="Connected example from methodology to methods">
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>1</span><strong>Methodology</strong><small>Which worldview fits?</small></summary>
                <p><strong>Positivist orientation</strong> — satisfaction is treated as a measurable pattern across learners.</p>
              </details>
              <span class="example-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>2</span><strong>Research design</strong><small>Which blueprint follows?</small></summary>
                <p><strong>Quantitative descriptive survey</strong> — estimates how satisfaction is distributed in the defined student population.</p>
              </details>
              <span class="example-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>3</span><strong>Methods</strong><small>Which tools provide the evidence?</small></summary>
                <p><strong>Structured questionnaire + descriptive statistics</strong> — Likert items; frequencies, percentages, mean and spread.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>三個相關但不同的決策</h2>
          <p class="decision-instruction">先閱讀每張卡片的問題，想好自己的答案，再點擊揭示。</p>
          <div class="decision-reveal-grid">
            <details class="decision-reveal" name="decision-level-zh">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">世界觀</span><h3>方法論</h3><p>甚麼算作知識？我們如何認識它？</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>廣泛而具哲學性。</strong>指導研究如何產生知識的世界觀與原則。</p><p class="decision-examples">實證主義 · 詮釋主義 · 建構主義 · 實用主義</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="decision-reveal decision-reveal--centre" name="decision-level-zh">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">藍圖</span><h3>研究設計</h3><p>研究應如何組織，才能回答研究問題？</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>策略性與結構性。</strong>把研究問題、證據、比較、時序與推論連結起來的計劃。</p><p class="decision-examples">實驗 · 描述性調查 · 相關研究 · 個案研究</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="decision-reveal" name="decision-level-zh">
              <summary><span class="decision-kicker">工具</span><h3>研究方法</h3><p>哪些程序能產生及分析所需證據？</p></summary>
              <div class="decision-answer"><p><strong>具體而實際。</strong>用來產生及分析資料的程序與技術。</p><p class="decision-examples">問卷 · 訪談 · 觀察 · 統計分析</p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
          <div class="connected-example">
            <div class="connected-example-head"><span>一項研究，三個對齊的選擇</span><p><strong>例題：</strong>中學生對人工智能輔助回饋的滿意程度如何？</p></div>
            <div class="example-chain" aria-label="從方法論到研究方法的連貫例子">
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>1</span><strong>方法論</strong><small>哪種世界觀合適？</small></summary>
                <p><strong>實證主義取向</strong>——把滿意度視為可在學習者群體中測量的模式。</p>
              </details>
              <span class="example-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>2</span><strong>研究設計</strong><small>由此需要哪種藍圖？</small></summary>
                <p><strong>量化描述性調查設計</strong>——估計已界定學生群體中滿意度的分布。</p>
              </details>
              <span class="example-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <details class="example-step">
                <summary><span>3</span><strong>研究方法</strong><small>哪些工具提供證據？</small></summary>
                <p><strong>結構式問卷＋描述統計</strong>——Likert 題項；頻數、百分比、平均數與離散程度。</p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Start with the intended claim" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Claim-led design</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What kind of answer are you seeking?</h2>
          <div class="claim-ladder design-claims">
            <article><span>Describe</span><p>What exists, how often, for whom or in what form?</p></article>
            <article><span>Relate</span><p>Do variables, conditions or experiences vary together?</p></article>
            <article><span>Explain</span><p>How or why does a process, pattern or experience occur?</p></article>
            <article><span>Evaluate change</span><p>Did an intervention or condition contribute to an outcome?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The wording of the claim determines what comparison, variation, context and evidence the design must provide.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>你要尋找哪一類答案？</h2>
          <div class="claim-ladder design-claims">
            <article><span>描述</span><p>存在甚麼、頻率如何、涉及誰，或呈現甚麼形式？</p></article>
            <article><span>關聯</span><p>變項、條件或經驗是否共同變化？</p></article>
            <article><span>解釋</span><p>某個過程、模式或經驗如何或為何發生？</p></article>
            <article><span>評估改變</span><p>某項介入或條件是否促成結果？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">主張的措辭決定研究設計必須提供甚麼比較、變異、情境與證據。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Design family map" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design landscape</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Begin with the question, not a favourite method</h2>
          <div class="design-family-map">
            <article><span>Pattern or estimate</span><strong>Descriptive / survey</strong></article>
            <article><span>Association or prediction</span><strong>Correlational</strong></article>
            <article><span>Difference or effect</span><strong>Experimental / quasi-experimental</strong></article>
            <article><span>Bounded complexity</span><strong>Case study</strong></article>
            <article><span>Meaning or experience</span><strong>Phenomenology / narrative</strong></article>
            <article><span>Culture, process or change</span><strong>Ethnography / grounded theory / action research</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">These are families, not recipes. Each still requires decisions about context, sampling, evidence, timing and quality.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>從研究問題出發，而不是從偏好的方法出發</h2>
          <div class="design-family-map">
            <article><span>模式或估計</span><strong>描述性研究／調查</strong></article>
            <article><span>關聯或預測</span><strong>相關研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>差異或效果</span><strong>實驗／準實驗研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>有邊界的複雜性</span><strong>個案研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>意義或經驗</span><strong>現象學／敘事研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>文化、過程或改變</span><strong>民族誌／紮根理論／行動研究</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">這些是設計類型，不是固定配方。每種設計仍需決定情境、抽樣、證據、時序及品質。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Interactive design family spider map" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design families · Explore one branch</span></header>
        <div data-language="en" data-design-family-map>
          <h2>One landscape, six design routes</h2>
          <p class="family-map-instruction">Choose the bubble that best matches the intended claim. Its next layer will spread out below.</p>
          <div class="family-spider" aria-label="Six research design families">
            <svg class="family-spider-lines" viewBox="0 0 1000 240" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M500 120 150 46M500 120 500 38M500 120 850 46M500 120 150 194M500 120 500 202M500 120 850 194" /></svg>
            <div class="family-spider-core"><span>Research<br />question</span><small>intended claim</small></div>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--1" type="button" data-family-select="descriptive-en" aria-controls="descriptive-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Descriptive / survey</strong><small>Pattern or estimate</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--2" type="button" data-family-select="correlational-en" aria-controls="correlational-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Correlational</strong><small>Association or prediction</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--3" type="button" data-family-select="experimental-en" aria-controls="experimental-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Experimental / quasi</strong><small>Difference or effect</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--4" type="button" data-family-select="case-en" aria-controls="case-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Case study</strong><small>Bounded complexity</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--5" type="button" data-family-select="experience-en" aria-controls="experience-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Phenomenology / narrative</strong><small>Experience or story</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--6 family-bubble--long" type="button" data-family-select="process-en" aria-controls="process-en" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Ethnography / grounded theory / action research</strong><small>Culture, process or change</small></button>
          </div>
          <div class="family-detail" data-family-detail aria-live="polite">
            <p class="family-detail-prompt" data-family-prompt>Select a design-family bubble to examine its purpose, decisions, evidence and claim boundary.</p>
            <section class="family-branch" id="descriptive-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>Best suited to</h3><p>Prevalence, distributions, characteristics, attitudes or reported practices.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Design decisions</h3><p>Target population, sampling frame, measurement quality and response coverage.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 58V14M15 58H82"/><rect x="25" y="39" width="10" height="19"/><rect x="43" y="28" width="10" height="30"/><rect x="61" y="18" width="10" height="40"/></svg><strong>Describe</strong><small>a population or pattern</small></div>
              <article><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>A one-time survey can describe or associate; it usually cannot establish causation.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Ask</h3><p>Whom should the estimate represent, and does the achieved sample support that scope?</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="correlational-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>Best suited to</h3><p>Whether variables move together and whether one set helps predict another.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Design decisions</h3><p>Construct definition, temporal ordering, plausible confounders and a justified model.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 58 80 16"/><circle cx="24" cy="50" r="4"/><circle cx="38" cy="39" r="4"/><circle cx="51" cy="42" r="4"/><circle cx="64" cy="25" r="4"/><circle cx="77" cy="20" r="4"/></svg><strong>Relate</strong><small>variation and association</small></div>
              <article><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>Prediction is not automatically explanation; association is not automatically causation.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Ask</h3><p>Which alternative explanation could produce the same observed association?</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="experimental-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>Experiment</h3><p>Manipulates a condition and uses random assignment where feasible to strengthen comparability.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Quasi-experiment</h3><p>Examines an intervention without random assignment and addresses pre-existing differences.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="26" cy="25" r="12"/><circle cx="70" cy="25" r="12"/><path d="M38 25H56M52 20l6 5-6 5M22 51h52"/></svg><strong>Evaluate change</strong><small>comparison over time</small></div>
              <article><h3>Evidence</h3><p>Comparison, before/after evidence, implementation fidelity and alternative explanations.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>A pre-test and post-test alone do not prove that the intervention caused the change.</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="case-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>The case</h3><p>A person, programme, class, school, event or organisation.</p></article>
              <article><h3>The boundary</h3><p>Define the place, period, participants and activity included.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="16" y="10" width="64" height="52" rx="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="29" r="5"/><circle cx="59" cy="29" r="5"/><path d="M29 48h38"/></svg><strong>Bounded case</strong><small>understood in context</small></div>
              <article><h3>The evidence</h3><p>Use multiple relevant sources to understand the case, not merely one interview.</p></article>
              <article><h3>The claim</h3><p>Explain the case deeply; do not treat it as a statistical sample of all cases.</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="experience-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>Phenomenology</h3><p>Investigates the structure and meaning of a shared lived experience.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Narrative research</h3><p>Investigates how people construct experience through sequence, turning points and voice.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13 16h34v24H28l-9 9v-9h-6zM50 29h33v24H72l-9 9v-9H50z"/><path d="M20 24h20M20 31h14M57 37h19M57 44h13"/></svg><strong>Meaning</strong><small>experience or story</small></div>
              <article><h3>Shared method</h3><p>Both may use interviews, but the analytic object and intended account differ.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Ask</h3><p>Is the object the meaning of an experience, or how a life is organised as a story?</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="process-en" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>Ethnography</h3><p>Understands practices and meanings in a social setting through sustained engagement.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Grounded theory</h3><p>Develops a process-oriented account through iterative collection, comparison and analysis.</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M29 18a25 25 0 0 1 38 10M68 22l-1 9-9-2M67 54a25 25 0 0 1-38-10M28 50l1-9 9 2"/><circle cx="48" cy="36" r="8"/></svg><strong>Process</strong><small>culture, theory or change</small></div>
              <article><h3>Action research</h3><p>Improves practice through planned cycles of action, evidence and reflection with participants.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>The label must change how the study is organised; it is not a synonym for “qualitative.”</p></article>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant" data-design-family-map>
          <h2>一個研究版圖，六條設計路徑</h2>
          <p class="family-map-instruction">選擇最符合預期主張的氣泡；下一層心智圖會在下方展開。</p>
          <div class="family-spider" aria-label="六種研究設計類型">
            <svg class="family-spider-lines" viewBox="0 0 1000 240" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M500 120 150 46M500 120 500 38M500 120 850 46M500 120 150 194M500 120 500 202M500 120 850 194" /></svg>
            <div class="family-spider-core"><span>研究<br />問題</span><small>預期主張</small></div>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--1" type="button" data-family-select="descriptive-zh" aria-controls="descriptive-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>描述性研究／調查</strong><small>模式或估計</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--2" type="button" data-family-select="correlational-zh" aria-controls="correlational-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>相關研究</strong><small>關聯或預測</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--3" type="button" data-family-select="experimental-zh" aria-controls="experimental-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>實驗／準實驗研究</strong><small>差異或效果</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--4" type="button" data-family-select="case-zh" aria-controls="case-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>個案研究</strong><small>有邊界的複雜性</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--5" type="button" data-family-select="experience-zh" aria-controls="experience-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>現象學／敘事研究</strong><small>經驗或故事</small></button>
            <button class="family-bubble family-bubble--6" type="button" data-family-select="process-zh" aria-controls="process-zh" aria-pressed="false"><strong>民族誌／紮根理論／行動研究</strong><small>文化、過程或改變</small></button>
          </div>
          <div class="family-detail" data-family-detail aria-live="polite">
            <p class="family-detail-prompt" data-family-prompt>選擇一個研究設計氣泡，查看其目的、關鍵決策、證據及主張邊界。</p>
            <section class="family-branch" id="descriptive-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>適合回答</h3><p>盛行率、分布、特徵、態度或自陳實踐。</p></article>
              <article><h3>設計決策</h3><p>目標群體、抽樣框、測量品質及回應覆蓋程度。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 58V14M15 58H82"/><rect x="25" y="39" width="10" height="19"/><rect x="43" y="28" width="10" height="30"/><rect x="61" y="18" width="10" height="40"/></svg><strong>描述</strong><small>群體、狀況或模式</small></div>
              <article><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>一次性調查可以描述或分析關聯，但通常不能確立因果。</p></article>
              <article><h3>要問</h3><p>估計結果應代表誰？實際取得的樣本能否支持這個範圍？</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="correlational-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>適合回答</h3><p>變項是否共同變化，以及一組變項能否協助預測另一組變項。</p></article>
              <article><h3>設計決策</h3><p>構念定義、時間先後、可能的混淆因素及有理據的模型。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14 58 80 16"/><circle cx="24" cy="50" r="4"/><circle cx="38" cy="39" r="4"/><circle cx="51" cy="42" r="4"/><circle cx="64" cy="25" r="4"/><circle cx="77" cy="20" r="4"/></svg><strong>關聯</strong><small>變異與預測</small></div>
              <article><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>預測不等於解釋；關聯也不等於因果。</p></article>
              <article><h3>要問</h3><p>哪個其他解釋也可能產生同樣的關聯？</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="experimental-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>實驗研究</h3><p>操弄條件，並在可行情況下隨機分派，以提高組別可比較性。</p></article>
              <article><h3>準實驗研究</h3><p>在沒有隨機分派下檢視介入，並明確處理原有組別差異。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="26" cy="25" r="12"/><circle cx="70" cy="25" r="12"/><path d="M38 25H56M52 20l6 5-6 5M22 51h52"/></svg><strong>評估改變</strong><small>比較與時序</small></div>
              <article><h3>所需證據</h3><p>比較、前後證據、實施忠實度及其他解釋。</p></article>
              <article><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>只有前測與後測，並不足以證明介入造成改變。</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="case-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>個案</h3><p>個人、課程、班級、學校、事件或組織。</p></article>
              <article><h3>邊界</h3><p>界定納入的地點、時期、參與者與活動。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="16" y="10" width="64" height="52" rx="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="29" r="5"/><circle cx="59" cy="29" r="5"/><path d="M29 48h38"/></svg><strong>有邊界的個案</strong><small>置於情境中理解</small></div>
              <article><h3>證據</h3><p>使用多種相關來源理解個案，而不只是進行一次訪談。</p></article>
              <article><h3>主張</h3><p>深入解釋個案，不把個案當成所有個案的統計樣本。</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="experience-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>現象學</h3><p>探討共同生活經驗的結構與意義。</p></article>
              <article><h3>敘事研究</h3><p>探討人們如何透過時序、轉折點及聲音建構經驗。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M13 16h34v24H28l-9 9v-9h-6zM50 29h33v24H72l-9 9v-9H50z"/><path d="M20 24h20M20 31h14M57 37h19M57 44h13"/></svg><strong>意義</strong><small>經驗或故事</small></div>
              <article><h3>共同方法</h3><p>兩者都可能使用訪談，但分析對象與預期解釋不同。</p></article>
              <article><h3>要問</h3><p>研究對象是經驗的意義，還是生命如何組織成故事？</p></article>
            </section>
            <section class="family-branch" id="process-zh" data-family-branch hidden>
              <article><h3>民族誌</h3><p>透過持續參與，理解社會場域中的實踐與意義。</p></article>
              <article><h3>紮根理論</h3><p>透過反覆蒐集、比較及分析，發展過程導向的理論解釋。</p></article>
              <div class="family-branch-centre"><svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M29 18a25 25 0 0 1 38 10M68 22l-1 9-9-2M67 54a25 25 0 0 1-38-10M28 50l1-9 9 2"/><circle cx="48" cy="36" r="8"/></svg><strong>過程</strong><small>文化、理論或改變</small></div>
              <article><h3>行動研究</h3><p>與參與者透過行動、證據及反思循環研究並改善實踐。</p></article>
              <article><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>設計名稱必須改變研究的組織方式，不能只是「質性研究」的同義詞。</p></article>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Mixed methods: the entry question" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family · Preview only</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Does the problem require both forms of evidence?</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Quantitative contribution</h3><p>Magnitude, distribution, comparison, association or change.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Qualitative contribution</h3><p>Meaning, mechanism, experience, process or contextual explanation.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Integration requirement</h3><p>The strands must inform one another and support a combined inference.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Two datasets do not automatically make mixed-methods research. Use both only when a single approach leaves a consequential gap.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究課題是否同時需要兩種證據？</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>量化貢獻</h3><p>幅度、分布、比較、關聯或改變。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>質性貢獻</h3><p>意義、機制、經驗、過程或情境解釋。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>整合要求</h3><p>兩個研究部分必須互相提供資訊，並支持綜合推論。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">擁有兩組資料不等於混合方法研究。只有當單一取向留下重要缺口時，才應同時使用兩者。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Design decision path" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">A repeatable decision sequence</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Ask these questions in order</h2>
          <ol class="decision-list">
            <li><strong>What must be understood or claimed?</strong><span>Describe, relate, explain, evaluate or predict?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What variation or context must be observed?</strong><span>Across people, settings, conditions, events or time?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What comparison is necessary?</strong><span>No comparison, within-case, between groups, before/after or across phases?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What evidence could challenge the preferred answer?</strong><span>Plan for alternatives, negative cases and rival explanations.</span></li>
            <li><strong>What design can be implemented ethically and well?</strong><span>A modest coherent design is stronger than an ambitious incoherent one.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>依次提出這些問題</h2>
          <ol class="decision-list">
            <li><strong>研究必須理解或主張甚麼？</strong><span>描述、關聯、解釋、評估，還是預測？</span></li>
            <li><strong>必須觀察甚麼變異或情境？</strong><span>跨個人、場域、條件、事件，還是時間？</span></li>
            <li><strong>需要甚麼比較？</strong><span>不比較、個案內、組別間、前後，還是跨階段？</span></li>
            <li><strong>甚麼證據可能挑戰偏好的答案？</strong><span>預先考慮其他解釋、反例與負面個案。</span></li>
            <li><strong>哪個設計能在倫理上妥善實施？</strong><span>規模適中而連貫的設計，勝過宏大但失去對齊的設計。</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

