    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 3: Design Clinic" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 3</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Design Clinic</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Diagnose the problem before opening each card. Then compare your repair with the suggested response.</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A one-time survey concludes that AI use causes stronger research confidence.</summary><p>The design establishes association, not causal direction. Revise the claim or add temporal evidence, a defensible comparison and control of alternative explanations.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>Ten purposively selected interviewees are used to estimate university-wide prevalence.</summary><p>Information-rich purposive sampling can support depth, not a population estimate. Revise the question or adopt a probability-based sampling plan.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A survey and interviews are conducted, then reported in separate chapters and called mixed methods.</summary><p>The study is merely additive unless the strands answer connected questions and contribute to a planned combined inference.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>The paper says “case study” but never identifies the case or its boundary.</summary><p>Define the bounded case, context, period and units; explain why the case is informative and which evidence is needed to understand it.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A study selects grounded theory because it includes interview coding.</summary><p>Coding interviews does not make grounded theory. The design requires iterative sampling and analysis directed towards developing a theoretical account.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>The preferred design requires access that the researcher is unlikely to obtain.</summary><p>Feasibility is a design condition. Narrow the setting, change the unit or select an alternative design that can still answer the core question well.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究設計診所</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">打開卡片前先診斷問題，再把你的修正與建議答案比較。</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>一次性調查得出「使用人工智能會造成更強研究信心」的結論。</summary><p>該設計只能建立關聯，不能確立因果方向。應修訂主張，或加入時間證據、有理據的比較及對其他解釋的控制。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>以十名目的抽樣的受訪者估計全校盛行率。</summary><p>目的抽樣可取得資訊豐富的深度證據，但不能支持群體估計。應修訂問題，或採用以機率為基礎的抽樣計劃。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>研究同時進行問卷與訪談，分章報告後便稱為混合方法。</summary><p>若兩個部分沒有回答互相連結的問題，也沒有支持預先規劃的綜合推論，研究只是在方法上相加。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>論文稱為「個案研究」，卻沒有指出個案及其邊界。</summary><p>應界定有邊界的個案、情境、時期及分析單位；解釋個案為何有資訊價值，以及需要哪些證據理解它。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>研究因為包含訪談編碼而選擇紮根理論。</summary><p>編碼訪談並不等於紮根理論。該設計需要以發展理論解釋為目標，反覆進行抽樣與分析。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>偏好的設計需要研究者不太可能取得的場域進入權限。</summary><p>可行性是設計條件。應縮小場域、改變分析單位，或選擇仍能妥善回答核心問題的替代設計。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Sampling foundations" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Define what is being sampled before choosing how</h2>
          <div class="sampling-stack">
            <article><strong>Unit of analysis</strong><span>What entity will the claims describe?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Target population or phenomenon</strong><span>To whom or what should the claim apply?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Accessible population or field</strong><span>What can the researcher realistically reach?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Sampling frame and criteria</strong><span>How will eligible people, cases, texts, events or settings be identified?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Achieved sample</strong><span>Who or what actually contributes usable evidence?</span></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The sample is not always people. It may include classrooms, documents, interactions, events, sites or time periods.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>先界定抽取甚麼，再決定如何抽樣</h2>
          <div class="sampling-stack">
            <article><strong>分析單位</strong><span>主張將描述哪一種實體？</span></article>
            <article><strong>目標群體或現象</strong><span>主張應適用於誰或甚麼？</span></article>
            <article><strong>可接觸群體或場域</strong><span>研究者實際能接觸甚麼？</span></article>
            <article><strong>抽樣框與準則</strong><span>如何辨識符合資格的人、個案、文本、事件或場域？</span></article>
            <article><strong>實際樣本</strong><span>最終由誰或甚麼提供可用證據？</span></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">樣本不一定是人，也可以是課堂、文件、互動、事件、場域或時段。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Sampling methods map" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling map</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Two selection logics, eight visible methods</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Before clicking, explain how units would enter the sample. Then reveal the method’s selection move, visual pattern and claim limit.</p>
          <div class="sampling-explorer" data-sampling-explorer>
            <div class="sampling-map" aria-label="Interactive map of sampling methods">
              <div class="sampling-root"><strong>Sampling methods</strong><span>How will units enter?</span></div>
              <div class="sampling-families">
                <section class="sampling-family sampling-family-probability">
                  <header><strong>Probability</strong><span>Selection uses chance</span></header>
                  <div class="sampling-method-grid">
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="simple-random" aria-controls="sampling-en-simple-random" aria-pressed="false">Simple random</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="systematic" aria-controls="sampling-en-systematic" aria-pressed="false">Systematic</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="stratified" aria-controls="sampling-en-stratified" aria-pressed="false">Stratified</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="cluster" aria-controls="sampling-en-cluster" aria-pressed="false">Cluster</button>
                  </div>
                  <p class="sampling-more"><b>Also:</b> multistage · probability proportional to size</p>
                </section>
                <section class="sampling-family sampling-family-nonprobability">
                  <header><strong>Non-probability</strong><span>Selection uses access or criteria</span></header>
                  <div class="sampling-method-grid">
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="convenience" aria-controls="sampling-en-convenience" aria-pressed="false">Convenience</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="purposive" aria-controls="sampling-en-purposive" aria-pressed="false">Purposive</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="snowball" aria-controls="sampling-en-snowball" aria-pressed="false">Snowball</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="quota" aria-controls="sampling-en-quota" aria-pressed="false">Quota</button>
                  </div>
                  <p class="sampling-more"><b>Also:</b> voluntary response · theoretical · consecutive</p>
                </section>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sampling-detail-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sampling-detail-empty" data-sampling-empty><strong>Pause before revealing</strong><p>Choose one method and predict: who can enter, how they are selected, and what claim becomes defensible?</p></div>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-simple-random" data-sampling-panel="simple-random" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-left"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Simple random sampling: individuals are selected across the full population" /></div><header><span>Probability</span><h3>Simple random</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Give every unit an equal chance through a random mechanism.</p><p><b>Watch</b> A complete sampling frame is normally needed.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-systematic" data-sampling-panel="systematic" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-right"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Systematic sampling: individuals are selected at a regular interval" /></div><header><span>Probability</span><h3>Systematic</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Choose a random start, then select every kth unit from an ordered frame.</p><p><b>Watch</b> A hidden pattern in the list can distort the sample.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-stratified" data-sampling-panel="stratified" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-left"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Stratified sampling: individuals are selected from every subgroup" /></div><header><span>Probability</span><h3>Stratified</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Divide by a relevant characteristic, then randomly sample within every stratum.</p><p><b>Watch</b> The strata and allocation must fit the intended inference.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-cluster" data-sampling-panel="cluster" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-right"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Cluster sampling: entire natural groups are selected" /></div><header><span>Probability</span><h3>Cluster</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Randomly choose natural groups, then include or sample units inside them.</p><p><b>Watch</b> Differences between clusters increase uncertainty.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-convenience" data-sampling-panel="convenience" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-left"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Convenience sampling: the most accessible individuals enter the sample" /></div><header><span>Non-probability</span><h3>Convenience</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Recruit the units easiest for the researcher to reach.</p><p><b>Claim limit</b> Accessibility can create strong selection bias; do not assume population representativeness.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-purposive" data-sampling-panel="purposive" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-right"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Purposive sampling: information-rich participants are deliberately selected" /></div><header><span>Non-probability</span><h3>Purposive</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Deliberately choose information-rich cases using explicit criteria.</p><p><b>Claim limit</b> Supports depth about a phenomenon, not population prevalence.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-snowball" data-sampling-panel="snowball" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-left"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Snowball sampling: initial participants refer others in their networks" /></div><header><span>Non-probability</span><h3>Snowball</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Begin with seed participants who refer others in a hard-to-reach network.</p><p><b>Claim limit</b> Network ties shape who becomes visible and who remains missing.</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-en-quota" data-sampling-panel="quota" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-right"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="Quota sampling: predetermined subgroup totals are filled non-randomly" /></div><header><span>Non-probability</span><h3>Quota</h3></header><p><b>Selection move</b> Set subgroup targets, then recruit non-randomly until each quota is filled.</p><p><b>Claim limit</b> Composition is controlled, but selection within each quota is still non-random.</p></article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>兩種選取邏輯，八種可視方法</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">點選前，先解釋單位會如何進入樣本；再揭示該方法的選取動作、圖像模式及主張限制。</p>
          <div class="sampling-explorer" data-sampling-explorer>
            <div class="sampling-map" aria-label="抽樣方法互動圖">
              <div class="sampling-root"><strong>抽樣方法</strong><span>單位如何進入樣本？</span></div>
              <div class="sampling-families">
                <section class="sampling-family sampling-family-probability">
                  <header><strong>機率抽樣</strong><span>以機會機制選取</span></header>
                  <div class="sampling-method-grid">
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="simple-random" aria-controls="sampling-zh-simple-random" aria-pressed="false">簡單隨機</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="systematic" aria-controls="sampling-zh-systematic" aria-pressed="false">系統抽樣</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="stratified" aria-controls="sampling-zh-stratified" aria-pressed="false">分層抽樣</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="cluster" aria-controls="sampling-zh-cluster" aria-pressed="false">叢集抽樣</button>
                  </div>
                  <p class="sampling-more"><b>其他：</b>多階段抽樣 · 按規模比例抽樣</p>
                </section>
                <section class="sampling-family sampling-family-nonprobability">
                  <header><strong>非機率抽樣</strong><span>按可接觸性或準則選取</span></header>
                  <div class="sampling-method-grid">
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="convenience" aria-controls="sampling-zh-convenience" aria-pressed="false">便利抽樣</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="purposive" aria-controls="sampling-zh-purposive" aria-pressed="false">目的抽樣</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="snowball" aria-controls="sampling-zh-snowball" aria-pressed="false">滾雪球抽樣</button>
                    <button type="button" data-sampling-method="quota" aria-controls="sampling-zh-quota" aria-pressed="false">配額抽樣</button>
                  </div>
                  <p class="sampling-more"><b>其他：</b>自願回應 · 理論抽樣 · 連續抽樣</p>
                </section>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sampling-detail-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sampling-detail-empty" data-sampling-empty><strong>揭示前先停一停</strong><p>選擇一種方法並預測：誰可以加入、如何被選取，以及能支持甚麼主張？</p></div>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-simple-random" data-sampling-panel="simple-random" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-left"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="簡單隨機抽樣：從整個群體隨機選取個體" /></div><header><span>機率抽樣</span><h3>簡單隨機</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 透過隨機機制，讓每個單位擁有相同的入選機會。</p><p><b>注意</b> 通常需要涵蓋完整群體的抽樣框。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-systematic" data-sampling-panel="systematic" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-right"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="系統抽樣：按固定間隔選取個體" /></div><header><span>機率抽樣</span><h3>系統抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 隨機決定起點，再從有序名單每隔第 k 個單位抽取。</p><p><b>注意</b> 名單中的隱藏規律可能扭曲樣本。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-stratified" data-sampling-panel="stratified" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-left"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="分層抽樣：從每一子群中選取個體" /></div><header><span>機率抽樣</span><h3>分層抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 按重要特徵分層，再在每一層內隨機抽取。</p><p><b>注意</b> 分層方式及比例配置必須符合預期推論。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-cluster" data-sampling-panel="cluster" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-right"><img src={probabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="叢集抽樣：選取完整的自然群組" /></div><header><span>機率抽樣</span><h3>叢集抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 隨機選取自然群組，再納入或抽取群組內的單位。</p><p><b>注意</b> 叢集之間的差異會增加不確定性。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-convenience" data-sampling-panel="convenience" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-left"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="便利抽樣：最容易接觸的個體進入樣本" /></div><header><span>非機率抽樣</span><h3>便利抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 招募研究者最容易接觸的單位。</p><p><b>主張限制</b> 可接觸性可能造成強烈選擇偏差，不能假設樣本代表整個群體。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-purposive" data-sampling-panel="purposive" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-top-right"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="目的抽樣：刻意選取資訊豐富的參與者" /></div><header><span>非機率抽樣</span><h3>目的抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 按明確準則，刻意選取資訊豐富的個案。</p><p><b>主張限制</b> 支持深入理解現象，不支持估計群體盛行率。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-snowball" data-sampling-panel="snowball" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-left"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="滾雪球抽樣：最初參與者轉介其網絡中的其他人" /></div><header><span>非機率抽樣</span><h3>滾雪球抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 由種子參與者開始，透過轉介接觸難以接近的網絡。</p><p><b>主張限制</b> 網絡連結會決定誰被看見，以及誰仍然缺席。</p></article>
              <article class="sampling-detail-card" id="sampling-zh-quota" data-sampling-panel="quota" hidden><div class="sampling-crop crop-bottom-right"><img src={nonProbabilitySamplingVisual} width="702" height="638" alt="配額抽樣：以非隨機方式填滿預定的子群人數" /></div><header><span>非機率抽樣</span><h3>配額抽樣</h3></header><p><b>選取動作</b> 設定子群目標，再以非隨機方式招募，直至填滿每項配額。</p><p><b>主張限制</b> 樣本組成受到控制，但每項配額內仍不是隨機選取。</p></article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Sample adequacy" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling logic</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>There is no universal “good sample size”</h2>
          <p class="sample-size-intro">Begin with the claim. Select a route, predict which inputs matter, then reveal the calculation logic.</p>
          <div class="sample-size-sequence" aria-label="Sample size planning sequence"><span>Claim</span><b>→</b><span>Assumptions</span><b>→</b><span>Base n</span><b>→</b><span>Adjust</span><b>→</b><span>Recruit</span></div>
          <div class="sample-size-workbench" data-sample-size-explorer>
            <nav class="sample-size-routes" aria-label="Choose a sample size planning route">
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="proportion" aria-controls="sample-size-en-proportion" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Estimate a proportion</strong><span>Precision</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="comparison" aria-controls="sample-size-en-comparison" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Compare two groups</strong><span>Power</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="cluster" aria-controls="sample-size-en-cluster" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Clustered design</strong><span>Design effect</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="qualitative" aria-controls="sample-size-en-qualitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Qualitative study</strong><span>Information adequacy</span></button>
            </nav>
            <div class="sample-size-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sample-size-empty" data-sample-size-empty><strong>Pause before calculating</strong><p>Are you estimating a population value, detecting a difference, adjusting for grouped data, or seeking information-rich cases?</p></div>
              <article id="sample-size-en-proportion" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="proportion" hidden>
                <header><span>Precision route</span><h3>One population proportion</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>n₀ = z²p(1 − p) / e²</strong><small>z confidence · p expected proportion · e margin of error</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>Worked example</b> 95% confidence, p = .50 and e = .05 gives n₀ = 384.16 → <strong>385</strong>.</p><p><b>Finite population</b> If N = 1,000, n = n₀ / [1 + (n₀ − 1)/N] → <strong>278</strong>.</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">Valid for a simple random estimate of one proportion; then adjust for design and nonresponse.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-comparison" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="comparison" hidden>
                <header><span>Power route</span><h3>A minimum meaningful difference</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>n/group ≈ 2(z<sub>1−α/2</sub> + z<sub>1−β</sub>)²σ² / Δ²</strong><small>α false-positive risk · 1−β power · σ variation · Δ target difference</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>Worked example</b> α = .05, power = 80%, standardised effect d = .50 → about <strong>63 per group</strong>.</p><p><b>Recruitment target</b> 126 completers with 15% attrition: 126 / .85 → <strong>149 recruits</strong>.</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">Smaller effects, greater variation, lower take-up and unequal allocation usually increase the required n.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-cluster" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="cluster" hidden>
                <header><span>Design adjustment</span><h3>People share a classroom, school or site</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>DE = 1 + (m − 1)ρ</strong><small>m average cluster size · ρ intracluster correlation · adjusted n = base n × DE</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>Worked example</b> m = 25 and ρ = .05 gives DE = <strong>2.20</strong>.</p><p><b>Apply it</b> A base total of 126 becomes 126 × 2.20 → <strong>278</strong>, before attrition.</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">The number of independent clusters matters; adding clusters is often more useful than adding people within the same cluster.</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-en-qualitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="qualitative" hidden>
                <header><span>Information route</span><h3>No defensible universal formula</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band formula-band-text"><strong>Adequacy = fit to purpose + information richness + analytic depth</strong><small>Plan a reasoned range and a transparent stopping rule.</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>Plan from</b> design, participant specificity, variation sought, access, data quality and the depth of analysis.</p><p><b>Stop and justify</b> when additional cases no longer materially change the analysis, or when a design-specific adequacy criterion is met.</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">A pilot or resource ceiling can test feasibility, but neither alone demonstrates adequate evidence.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-takeaway">Shortcut formulas, lookup tables and “30 participants” are assumption-bound—not universal answers. Report the claim, inputs, unit, adjustments and final target.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>並不存在通用的「良好樣本量」</h2>
          <p class="sample-size-intro">先由研究主張出發。選擇路徑，預測哪些輸入條件重要，再揭示計算邏輯。</p>
          <div class="sample-size-sequence" aria-label="樣本量規劃流程"><span>主張</span><b>→</b><span>假設</span><b>→</b><span>基礎 n</span><b>→</b><span>調整</span><b>→</b><span>招募</span></div>
          <div class="sample-size-workbench" data-sample-size-explorer>
            <nav class="sample-size-routes" aria-label="選擇樣本量規劃路徑">
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="proportion" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-proportion" aria-pressed="false"><strong>估計一項比例</strong><span>精確度</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="comparison" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-comparison" aria-pressed="false"><strong>比較兩組</strong><span>統計功效</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="cluster" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-cluster" aria-pressed="false"><strong>叢集設計</strong><span>設計效應</span></button>
              <button type="button" data-sample-size-route="qualitative" aria-controls="sample-size-zh-qualitative" aria-pressed="false"><strong>質性研究</strong><span>資訊充分性</span></button>
            </nav>
            <div class="sample-size-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="sample-size-empty" data-sample-size-empty><strong>計算前先停一停</strong><p>你要估計群體數值、偵測差異、調整群組資料，還是尋找資訊豐富的個案？</p></div>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-proportion" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="proportion" hidden>
                <header><span>精確度路徑</span><h3>一項群體比例</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>n₀ = z²p(1 − p) / e²</strong><small>z 置信水平 · p 預期比例 · e 誤差範圍</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>計算例子</b> 95% 置信水平、p = .50、e = .05：n₀ = 384.16 → <strong>385</strong>。</p><p><b>有限群體</b> 若 N = 1,000，n = n₀ / [1 + (n₀ − 1)/N] → <strong>278</strong>。</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">適用於以簡單隨機樣本估計一項比例；其後仍須按研究設計及無回應作調整。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-comparison" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="comparison" hidden>
                <header><span>統計功效路徑</span><h3>可被視為有意義的最小差異</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>每組 n ≈ 2(z<sub>1−α/2</sub> + z<sub>1−β</sub>)²σ² / Δ²</strong><small>α 假陽性風險 · 1−β 功效 · σ 變異 · Δ 目標差異</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>計算例子</b> α = .05、功效 = 80%、標準化效果 d = .50 → 每組約 <strong>63 人</strong>。</p><p><b>招募目標</b> 126 名完成者、預計流失 15%：126 / .85 → <strong>招募 149 人</strong>。</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">效果較小、變異較大、參與率較低或分組不平均，通常都需要較大的 n。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-cluster" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="cluster" hidden>
                <header><span>設計調整</span><h3>參與者同屬班級、學校或場域</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band"><strong>DE = 1 + (m − 1)ρ</strong><small>m 平均叢集大小 · ρ 組內相關 · 調整後 n = 基礎 n × DE</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>計算例子</b> m = 25、ρ = .05，DE = <strong>2.20</strong>。</p><p><b>套用調整</b> 基礎總數 126 × 2.20 → <strong>278</strong>，尚未計入流失。</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">獨立叢集的數目很重要；增加叢集通常比只在同一叢集內增加人數更有用。</p>
              </article>
              <article id="sample-size-zh-qualitative" class="sample-size-panel" data-sample-size-panel="qualitative" hidden>
                <header><span>資訊路徑</span><h3>沒有站得住腳的通用公式</h3></header>
                <div class="formula-band formula-band-text"><strong>充分性 = 切合目的 + 資訊豐富度 + 分析深度</strong><small>規劃一個有理據的範圍及透明的停止準則。</small></div>
                <div class="sample-size-notes"><p><b>規劃依據</b> 研究設計、參與者特定性、所需差異、可接觸性、資料品質及分析深度。</p><p><b>停止與論證</b> 當新增個案不再實質改變分析，或已符合該設計的充分性準則。</p></div>
                <p class="sample-size-caution">先導研究或資源上限可檢驗可行性，但兩者本身都不能證明證據充分。</p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="sample-size-takeaway">捷徑公式、查表及「30 人」都受假設限制，並非通用答案。應報告主張、輸入條件、抽樣單位、各項調整及最終目標。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 4: Sampling Match" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 4</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Sampling Match</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Match the selection procedure to the sampling strategy.</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Randomly select four schools, then randomly select students within each school.</p><select data-answer="multistage"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Select teachers who have implemented bilingual assessment for at least two years.</p><select data-answer="purposive"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Randomly sample within school level so primary and secondary schools are both represented.</p><select data-answer="stratified"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Ask participants in a hard-to-reach professional network to refer eligible colleagues.</p><select data-answer="snowball"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check matches</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>抽樣配對</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">把選取程序配對至相應抽樣策略。</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>隨機選取四所學校，再於每所學校內隨機抽取學生。</p><select data-answer="multistage"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>選取已有至少兩年雙語評估實施經驗的教師。</p><select data-answer="purposive"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>在不同學校階段內隨機抽樣，以確保小學與中學均有代表。</p><select data-answer="stratified"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>請難以接觸的專業網絡中的參與者轉介符合資格的同事。</p><select data-answer="snowball"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查配對</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Evidence to claim" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research quality</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Quality asks whether the inference is warranted</h2>
          <div class="path-line quality-chain">
            <span>Question</span><b>→</b><span>Evidence</span><b>→</b><span>Analysis</span><b>→</b><span>Claim</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3 quality-questions">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Accuracy</h3><p>Does the evidence represent the intended construct, experience or process?</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Alternatives</h3><p>Could bias, confounding, selection or interpretation produce another account?</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Boundary</h3><p>How far beyond these participants, cases, conditions and measures may the claim travel?</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究品質關乎推論是否有充分理據</h2>
          <div class="path-line quality-chain">
            <span>研究問題</span><b>→</b><span>證據</span><b>→</b><span>分析</span><b>→</b><span>主張</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3 quality-questions">
            <article class="panel"><h3>準確性</h3><p>證據是否代表研究所指的構念、經驗或過程？</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>其他解釋</h3><p>偏誤、混淆、選取或詮釋是否可能產生另一種解釋？</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>邊界</h3><p>主張能在多大程度上超出這些參與者、個案、條件與測量？</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Validity and reliability" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Quantitative quality</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Different threats require different safeguards</h2>
          <p class="validity-intro">First distinguish hitting the intended target from producing a consistent pattern.</p>
          <div class="validity-workbench" data-validity-workbench>
            <nav class="validity-tabs" aria-label="Validity and reliability learning sequence">
              <button type="button" data-validity-tab="targets" aria-controls="validity-en-targets" aria-pressed="true">1 · Read the targets</button>
              <button type="button" data-validity-tab="terms" aria-controls="validity-en-terms" aria-pressed="false">2 · Map the terms</button>
            </nav>
            <section id="validity-en-targets" class="validity-panel" data-validity-panel="targets">
              <div class="target-patterns">
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Shots are dispersed and away from the centre: neither reliable nor valid">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="20" cy="27" r="3"/><circle cx="31" cy="18" r="3"/><circle cx="43" cy="34" r="3"/><circle cx="55" cy="17" r="3"/><circle cx="69" cy="29" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="16" r="3"/><circle cx="94" cy="32" r="3"/><circle cx="27" cy="45" r="3"/><circle cx="73" cy="43" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>Neither</strong><span>Scattered and off target</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Shots are dispersed around the centre: accurate on average but unreliable">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="22" cy="56" r="3"/><circle cx="34" cy="30" r="3"/><circle cx="58" cy="25" r="3"/><circle cx="86" cy="35" r="3"/><circle cx="96" cy="62" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="88" r="3"/><circle cx="52" cy="96" r="3"/><circle cx="31" cy="79" r="3"/><circle cx="66" cy="64" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>Valid on average</strong><span>Centred but inconsistent</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Shots form a tight cluster away from the centre: reliable but invalid">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="82" cy="35" r="3"/><circle cx="88" cy="38" r="3"/><circle cx="84" cy="42" r="3"/><circle cx="91" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="78" cy="43" r="3"/><circle cx="86" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="94" cy="37" r="3"/><circle cx="81" cy="31" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>Reliable, not valid</strong><span>Consistent systematic bias</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Shots form a tight cluster at the centre: reliable and valid">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="55" cy="55" r="3"/><circle cx="62" cy="53" r="3"/><circle cx="67" cy="58" r="3"/><circle cx="58" cy="62" r="3"/><circle cx="64" cy="65" r="3"/><circle cx="53" cy="67" r="3"/><circle cx="60" cy="59" r="3"/><circle cx="68" cy="68" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>Reliable and valid</strong><span>Consistent and on target</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
              <div class="validity-definitions"><p><strong>Reliability asks:</strong> Do repeated scores or observations cluster together?</p><p><strong>Validity asks:</strong> Do the evidence and inference hit the intended target?</p></div>
              <p class="validity-note">The target is a teaching analogy: validity also concerns constructs, causal explanations, generalisation and statistical conclusions.</p>
            </section>
            <section id="validity-en-terms" class="validity-panel" data-validity-panel="terms" hidden>
              <div class="quality-map-core"><strong>Research quality</strong><span>What makes this inference or interpretation defensible?</span></div>
              <div class="quality-terminology-map">
                <section class="quality-map-branch quality-map-quant">
                  <header><span>Quantitative studies</span><h3>Validity + reliability</h3></header>
                  <div class="quality-map-nodes">{quantitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <article><strong>{term.labelEn}</strong><span>{term.mapEn}</span></article>)}</div>
                  <p>Older “internal/external reliability” labels are clearer when unpacked as consistency, stability, equivalence and rater agreement.</p>
                </section>
                <div class="quality-map-bridge"><strong>Related questions</strong><span>not one-to-one translations</span></div>
                <section class="quality-map-branch quality-map-qual">
                  <header><span>Qualitative studies</span><h3>Trustworthiness + methodological integrity</h3></header>
                  <div class="quality-map-nodes">{qualitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <article><strong>{term.labelEn}</strong><span>{term.mapEn}</span></article>)}</div>
                  <p>Dependability is not test-retest reliability; transferability is not statistical generalisability. Each answers a different quality question.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="quality-map-footer"><strong>Across the whole study:</strong> make decisions transparent from collection → processing → analysis → reporting; usefulness follows only when claims are methodologically supported.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>不同威脅需要不同保障</h2>
          <p class="validity-intro">首先區分是否擊中預期目標，以及是否產生一致的結果模式。</p>
          <div class="validity-workbench" data-validity-workbench>
            <nav class="validity-tabs" aria-label="效度與信度學習次序">
              <button type="button" data-validity-tab="targets" aria-controls="validity-zh-targets" aria-pressed="true">1 · 閱讀靶圖</button>
              <button type="button" data-validity-tab="terms" aria-controls="validity-zh-terms" aria-pressed="false">2 · 繪製術語圖</button>
            </nav>
            <section id="validity-zh-targets" class="validity-panel" data-validity-panel="targets">
              <div class="target-patterns">
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="落點分散並偏離中心：既不可靠也無效">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="20" cy="27" r="3"/><circle cx="31" cy="18" r="3"/><circle cx="43" cy="34" r="3"/><circle cx="55" cy="17" r="3"/><circle cx="69" cy="29" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="16" r="3"/><circle cx="94" cy="32" r="3"/><circle cx="27" cy="45" r="3"/><circle cx="73" cy="43" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>兩者皆無</strong><span>分散且偏離目標</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="落點散布於中心四周：平均準確但不可靠">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="22" cy="56" r="3"/><circle cx="34" cy="30" r="3"/><circle cx="58" cy="25" r="3"/><circle cx="86" cy="35" r="3"/><circle cx="96" cy="62" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="88" r="3"/><circle cx="52" cy="96" r="3"/><circle cx="31" cy="79" r="3"/><circle cx="66" cy="64" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>平均而言具效度</strong><span>居中但不一致</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="落點緊密但偏離中心：可靠但無效">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="82" cy="35" r="3"/><circle cx="88" cy="38" r="3"/><circle cx="84" cy="42" r="3"/><circle cx="91" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="78" cy="43" r="3"/><circle cx="86" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="94" cy="37" r="3"/><circle cx="81" cy="31" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>有信度、無效度</strong><span>一致的系統偏誤</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="落點緊密集中於中心：可靠而有效">
                    <g class="target-board"><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="36"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="24"/><circle cx="60" cy="60" r="12"/><path d="M8 60h104M60 8v104"/></g>
                    <g class="target-shots"><circle cx="55" cy="55" r="3"/><circle cx="62" cy="53" r="3"/><circle cx="67" cy="58" r="3"/><circle cx="58" cy="62" r="3"/><circle cx="64" cy="65" r="3"/><circle cx="53" cy="67" r="3"/><circle cx="60" cy="59" r="3"/><circle cx="68" cy="68" r="3"/></g>
                  </svg>
                  <figcaption><strong>有信度亦有效度</strong><span>一致且擊中目標</span></figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
              <div class="validity-definitions"><p><strong>信度問：</strong>重複得到的分數或觀察是否彼此接近？</p><p><strong>效度問：</strong>證據及推論是否擊中研究所指的目標？</p></div>
              <p class="validity-note">靶圖只是一個教學比喻：效度亦涉及構念、因果解釋、推廣範圍及統計結論。</p>
            </section>
            <section id="validity-zh-terms" class="validity-panel" data-validity-panel="terms" hidden>
              <div class="quality-map-core"><strong>研究品質</strong><span>甚麼使這項推論或詮釋站得住腳？</span></div>
              <div class="quality-terminology-map">
                <section class="quality-map-branch quality-map-quant">
                  <header><span>量化研究</span><h3>效度 + 信度</h3></header>
                  <div class="quality-map-nodes">{quantitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <article><strong>{term.labelZh}</strong><span>{term.mapZh}</span></article>)}</div>
                  <p>與其使用較含糊的「內部／外部信度」，不如拆解為一致性、穩定性、等值性及評分者一致。</p>
                </section>
                <div class="quality-map-bridge"><strong>相關問題</strong><span>並非逐一對譯</span></div>
                <section class="quality-map-branch quality-map-qual">
                  <header><span>質性研究</span><h3>可信賴性 + 方法完整性</h3></header>
                  <div class="quality-map-nodes">{qualitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <article><strong>{term.labelZh}</strong><span>{term.mapZh}</span></article>)}</div>
                  <p>依賴性不等於重測信度，可轉移性亦不等於統計推廣；每個術語回答不同的品質問題。</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="quality-map-footer"><strong>貫穿整項研究：</strong>使決策由蒐集 → 處理 → 分析 → 報告均透明可見；只有主張得到方法支持，研究結果才可能有用。</p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Quality safeguards explorer" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Quality in action</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Move from a quality threat to a safeguard</h2>
          <p class="quality-explorer-intro">Choose a term. Identify what convincing evidence would look like, name the issue, then select techniques that address that issue.</p>
          <div class="quality-explorer" data-quality-explorer>
            <div class="quality-term-selector">
              <section><header><strong>Quantitative</strong><span>measurement + inference</span></header><div>{quantitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <button type="button" data-quality-term={term.id} aria-controls={`quality-en-${term.id}`} aria-pressed="false">{term.labelEn}</button>)}</div></section>
              <section><header><strong>Qualitative</strong><span>interpretation + process</span></header><div>{qualitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <button type="button" data-quality-term={term.id} aria-controls={`quality-en-${term.id}`} aria-pressed="false">{term.labelEn}</button>)}</div></section>
            </div>
            <div class="quality-guidance-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="quality-guidance-empty" data-quality-empty><strong>No strategy is an automatic certificate</strong><p>Predict the threat first. A technique improves quality only when it fits the design and addresses that named threat.</p></div>
              {qualityTerms.map((term) => (
                <article id={`quality-en-${term.id}`} class="quality-guidance" data-quality-panel={term.id} hidden>
                  <header><span>{term.family === 'quant' ? 'Quantitative quality' : 'Qualitative quality'}</span><h3>{term.labelEn}</h3></header>
                  <button class="quality-reset" type="button" data-quality-reset>← All terms</button>
                  <dl><div><dt>Indicator</dt><dd>{term.indicatorEn}</dd></div><div><dt>Issue</dt><dd>{term.issueEn}</dd></div></dl>
                  <div class="quality-strategies"><strong>Safeguards to consider</strong><ul>{term.strategiesEn.map((strategy) => <li>{strategy}</li>)}</ul></div>
                </article>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="quality-explorer-footer">Document why each safeguard fits the claim, design and threat—not merely that it was used.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>由品質威脅走向保障策略</h2>
          <p class="quality-explorer-intro">選擇一個術語。先辨識具說服力的證據、說明問題，再選取真正處理該問題的技巧。</p>
          <div class="quality-explorer" data-quality-explorer>
            <div class="quality-term-selector">
              <section><header><strong>量化研究</strong><span>測量 + 推論</span></header><div>{quantitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <button type="button" data-quality-term={term.id} aria-controls={`quality-zh-${term.id}`} aria-pressed="false">{term.labelZh}</button>)}</div></section>
              <section><header><strong>質性研究</strong><span>詮釋 + 過程</span></header><div>{qualitativeQualityTerms.map((term) => <button type="button" data-quality-term={term.id} aria-controls={`quality-zh-${term.id}`} aria-pressed="false">{term.labelZh}</button>)}</div></section>
            </div>
            <div class="quality-guidance-stage" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="quality-guidance-empty" data-quality-empty><strong>沒有任何策略可以自動保證品質</strong><p>先預測威脅。只有技巧符合研究設計並處理已命名的威脅，才可能提升品質。</p></div>
              {qualityTerms.map((term) => (
                <article id={`quality-zh-${term.id}`} class="quality-guidance" data-quality-panel={term.id} hidden>
                  <header><span>{term.family === 'quant' ? '量化研究品質' : '質性研究品質'}</span><h3>{term.labelZh}</h3></header>
                  <button class="quality-reset" type="button" data-quality-reset>← 所有術語</button>
                  <dl><div><dt>指標</dt><dd>{term.indicatorZh}</dd></div><div><dt>問題</dt><dd>{term.issueZh}</dd></div></dl>
                  <div class="quality-strategies"><strong>可考慮的保障策略</strong><ul>{term.strategiesZh.map((strategy) => <li>{strategy}</li>)}</ul></div>
                </article>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="quality-explorer-footer">記錄每項保障為何符合研究主張、設計及威脅，而不只是列出曾經使用。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Mixed-methods quality" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Preview only</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Each strand can be sound while the whole remains weak</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Appropriateness</h3><p>Does each strand answer a necessary part of the research question?</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Consistency</h3><p>Do design, sampling and analysis support the same overall purpose?</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Connection</h3><p>Are the strands connected where the design says they will be?</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Combined inference</h3><p>Does integration produce an answer that neither strand could provide alone?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The detailed integration procedures belong to the later mixed-methods lesson. Today, identify whether integration is genuinely required.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>每個研究部分都可以穩健，但整體研究仍可能薄弱</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>合適性</h3><p>每個部分是否回答研究問題中不可缺少的一部分？</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>一致性</h3><p>設計、抽樣及分析是否支持相同的整體目的？</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>連結</h3><p>不同部分是否在設計所規劃的位置互相連結？</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>綜合推論</h3><p>整合是否產生任何單一部分都無法獨立提供的答案？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">具體整合程序留待之後的混合方法課。今天只需判斷研究是否真正需要整合。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 5: Quality Match" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 5</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Quality Match</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Match each safeguard or threat to the quality criterion it addresses most directly.</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Groups differ before the intervention and no adjustment or comparison is made.</p><select data-answer="internal"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="internal">Internal validity</option><option value="reliability">Reliability</option><option value="credibility">Credibility</option><option value="transfer">Transferability</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Two raters apply a scoring rubric inconsistently.</p><select data-answer="reliability"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="internal">Internal validity</option><option value="reliability">Reliability</option><option value="credibility">Credibility</option><option value="transfer">Transferability</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Interpretations are tested against contrary cases and supported with low-inference evidence.</p><select data-answer="credibility"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="internal">Internal validity</option><option value="reliability">Reliability</option><option value="credibility">Credibility</option><option value="transfer">Transferability</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>The report richly describes the setting and participants so readers can judge contextual relevance.</p><select data-answer="transfer"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="internal">Internal validity</option><option value="reliability">Reliability</option><option value="credibility">Credibility</option><option value="transfer">Transferability</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check matches</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究品質配對</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">把每項保障或威脅配對至它最直接處理的品質準則。</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>介入前各組已存在差異，研究卻沒有調整或作出比較。</p><select data-answer="internal"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="internal">內部效度</option><option value="reliability">信度</option><option value="credibility">可信性</option><option value="transfer">可轉移性</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>兩名評分者以不一致方式使用評分規準。</p><select data-answer="reliability"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="internal">內部效度</option><option value="reliability">信度</option><option value="credibility">可信性</option><option value="transfer">可轉移性</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>研究以反例檢驗詮釋，並以低推論證據加以支持。</p><select data-answer="credibility"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="internal">內部效度</option><option value="reliability">信度</option><option value="credibility">可信性</option><option value="transfer">可轉移性</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>報告豐富描述場域與參與者，使讀者能判斷其他情境的相關性。</p><select data-answer="transfer"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="internal">內部效度</option><option value="reliability">信度</option><option value="credibility">可信性</option><option value="transfer">可轉移性</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查配對</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Methodological alignment" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The whole-study test</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Every decision must serve the same study</h2>
          <div class="alignment-flow">
            <span>Problem</span><b>→</b><span>Framework</span><b>→</b><span>Question</span><b>→</b><span>Claim</span><b>→</b><span>Design</span><b>→</b><span>Sample</span><b>→</b><span>Evidence</span><b>→</b><span>Quality</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Alignment gives every research choice a clear, visible role in answering the research question.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>每項決策都必須服務同一研究</h2>
          <div class="alignment-flow">
            <span>課題</span><b>→</b><span>框架</span><b>→</b><span>問題</span><b>→</b><span>主張</span><b>→</b><span>設計</span><b>→</b><span>樣本</span><b>→</b><span>證據</span><b>→</b><span>品質</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">對齊並不表示所有元素都相同，而是每項選擇在回答研究問題時都有可見功能。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Peer Alignment Audit" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Peer review</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Audit the chain, not the topic</h2>
          <div class="audit-grid">
            <article><span>1</span><p>Does the framework genuinely shape the question?</p></article>
            <article><span>2</span><p>Does the design permit the intended claim?</p></article>
            <article><span>3</span><p>Will the sampling logic produce the required evidence?</p></article>
            <article><span>4</span><p>Is the design feasible in the available context?</p></article>
            <article><span>5</span><p>Does the quality safeguard address the main threat?</p></article>
            <article><span>6</span><p>Which word in the claim needs tighter boundaries?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Give one precise diagnosis and one feasible repair. “Looks good” is not methodological feedback.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>審視對齊，而不是評論研究主題</h2>
          <div class="audit-grid">
            <article><span>1</span><p>框架是否真正影響研究問題？</p></article>
            <article><span>2</span><p>研究設計是否容許預期主張？</p></article>
            <article><span>3</span><p>抽樣邏輯能否產生所需證據？</p></article>
            <article><span>4</span><p>研究設計在現有情境中是否可行？</p></article>
            <article><span>5</span><p>品質保障是否處理最主要威脅？</p></article>
            <article><span>6</span><p>主張中的哪個詞需要更嚴格的邊界？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">提出一項精確診斷及一項可行修正。「看起來不錯」並不是方法論回饋。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Exit ticket" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Exit ticket</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Make one decision defensible</h2>
          <div class="writing-grid exit-writing">
            <label>My strongest alignment decision<textarea data-save="exit-decision" placeholder="State the decision and why it fits the rest of the study."></textarea></label>
            <label>My next unresolved decision<textarea data-save="exit-next" placeholder="State what must be decided before instruments or ethics materials can be developed."></textarea></label>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A defensible study makes its logic visible before data collection begins.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>使一項決策站得住腳</h2>
          <div class="writing-grid exit-writing">
            <label>我最穩健的對齊決策<textarea data-save="exit-decision-zh" placeholder="說明該項決策，以及它為何符合研究的其他部分。"></textarea></label>
            <label>我下一項尚未解決的決策<textarea data-save="exit-next-zh" placeholder="說明在發展研究工具或倫理材料前必須決定甚麼。"></textarea></label>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">一項站得住腳的研究，會在蒐集資料前使其邏輯清晰可見。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Personal PDF" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner title-slide">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Keep your work</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h1>Keep the<br />chain intact</h1>
          <p class="lead">Save the lesson and your Study Architecture responses as a personal PDF.</p>
          <div class="closing-actions"><button type="button" class="pdf-cta" data-pdf-open>Create your personal PDF</button><a class="course-return" href={courseHref}>DEDC02 course materials</a></div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h1>保持<br />邏輯連結</h1>
          <p class="lead">把本課內容及研究架構回應儲存為個人 PDF。</p>
          <div class="closing-actions"><button type="button" class="pdf-cta" data-pdf-open>建立你的個人 PDF</button><a class="course-return" href={courseHref}>DEDC02 課程材料</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
